      <div type="clause" n="18.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 18.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18.1" corresp="#wit-e"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.32"/><pb n="58" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif beweddodu<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.33"/> fæmne hie forlicgge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.34"/>, gif hio sie cirlisc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.35"/>, mid LX scill. gebete þam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.36"/> byrgean<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.37"/>, ⁊ þæt sie on cwicæhtum feogodum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.1"/>, ⁊ mon nænigne mon on ðæt ne selle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="58" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif beweddod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.12"/> fæmne hy forlicge, gif heo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.7"/> sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.4"/> cierlisc, mid LX scll' gebete ða<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.13"/> hit gebyrie, ⁊ ðæt sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.1-2"/> on cwicæhtum feogodum, ⁊ mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.2"/> nænigne mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.2"/> on ðæt ne sylle.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.1-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18.1" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="58" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf beweddod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.7-2"/> fæmne héo forlicge, gyf héo sy ceorlisc, syxtig scill' gebete ðam þe hit gebyrige, ⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> sy on cwycæhtu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> feogodu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>, ⁊ man næningne man on þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ne sylle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="18.1" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.22"/><pb n="59" ed="#liebermann"/>Si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.23"/> desponsata femina fornicetur et cirlisca sit, LX solid. emendetur marito, et hoc in uiuente captali<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.1-3"/> componatur, et nemo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.2-2"/> uendatur in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.oe.3"/> (pro) eo.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="72" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif beweddodu<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#Af_18-1.attnote.fn.12"/> fæmne hie forlicgge, gif hio sie cirlisc, mid LX scill. gebete þam byrgean<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#Af_18-1.attnote.fn.13"/>, ⁊ þæt sie on cwicæhtum feogodum, ⁊ mon nænigne<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#Af_18-1.attnote.fn.14"/> mon on ðæt ne selle.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="21" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="312" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif beweddodu fæmne hie forlicgge, gif hio sie cirlisc, mid LX scill gebete þam byrgean, ⁊ þæt sie on cwicæhtum feogodum, ⁊ mon nænigne mon on ðæt ne selle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="59" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.de.1"/> eine verlobte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.de.2"/> Jungfrau sich beschlafen lässt, so büsse sie, wenn sie gemeinfrei ist, dem [Verlobungs]bürgen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.de.3"/> mit 60 Schilling<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.de.4"/>, und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.de.5"/> dies [Bussgeld] bestehe in Lebgütern, Werthgegenständen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.de.6"/>; und man veräussere dabei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.de.7"/> keinen [unfreien] Menschen.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_18-1.lnote.de.8"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a betrothed girl lets herself be lain with, then, if she is of common-free rank, let her pay the [betrothal-]surety 60 shillings, and let this [compensation] consist of livestock, goods of value; and let no [unfree] person be given away in it.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="73" ed="#attenborough"/>If a young woman who is betrothed commits fornication, she shall pay compensation to the amount of 60 shillings to the surety<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_18-1.attnote.n.1"/> [of the marriage], if she is a commoner. This sum shall be [paid] in livestock, cattle<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Af_18-1.attnote.n.2"/> being the property tendered, and no slave shall be given in such a payment.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="412" ed="#whitelock"/>If a betrothed maiden commits fornication, if she is of <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> birth, 60 shillings compensation is to be paid to the surety; and it is to be paid in livestock, cattle<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_18-1.whinote.n.1"/> [only], and one is not to include in it any slave.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="313" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a contractually betrothed woman fornicates [with someone other than her intended husband], if she is of <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> rank, let her compensate the guarantor [to the marriage] with 60 shillings, and that must be in livestock, and no person [in servitude] can be given for that.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="280"><label>cf. (wergeld enumerations)</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_70">Ine 70</ref> <quote>Alfred enumerated the wergelds ... five times as against Ine's once (n. 80)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_10">Abt 10–11</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_14">Abt 14</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_16">Abt 16</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_31">Abt 31</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_82">Abt 82–85</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="313"><label>contrast</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_54-1">Ine 54.1</ref> <quote>Ine §57.1 allows a slave to be given as part of a wergild payment.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="313"><label>see</label> <ref target="clause:Wif_6">Wif 6</ref> <quote>Namely, the one who gave surety for the completion of the marriage contract. See Wifmannes Beweddung §6.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="253"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-29">Af El 29</ref> <quote>Cf. Alfred §21, where it is established that a betrothed woman who fornicates with someone other than her intended husband is obligated to compensate the guarantor</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="309"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_11-4">Af 11.4</ref> <quote>Cf. Alfred §21.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="419"><label>contrast</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_54-1">Ine 54.1</ref> <quote>Alfred §21 requires a fine paid in livestock, but specifically prohibits the substitution of a slave.</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_18-1.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">18, 1. 2. 3 <hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld; vgl. Quadr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">18, 1. 2. 3 lacking in Ld; cf. Quadr.</seg></note>
